---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Privacy Policy | defamationcalc.com';
const description = 'Privacy policy for defamationcalc.com — how we collect, use, and share visitor data, including the case-review form, Google AdSense, and Google Analytics.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> July 2026.</p>
  <p>defamationcalc.com is committed to operating transparently with respect to data collection. This policy explains what information is collected when you use this site, how it is used, who it is shared with, and what choices you have.</p>

  <h2>Who We Are</h2>
  <p>defamationcalc.com is operated by The Click Lab Agency LLC (business email: <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>). We operate a portfolio of free legal and financial reference websites monetized through Google AdSense display advertising and, on this site, an optional case-review form.</p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>Browsing defamationcalc.com — using the calculator or reading the guides — does not collect any personal information. No account, registration, or comment section exists, and calculator inputs (plaintiff type, defendant type, per se selection, actual malice selection, damages amount) are processed entirely in the visitor's browser using JavaScript. No calculator inputs are transmitted to our servers or to any third party.</p>
  <p>If you submit the Defamation case-review form on our homepage, we collect your name, phone number, email address, the case details you enter, and a timestamp of your consent. That information is only collected if you choose to submit the form.</p>
  <p>Beyond the form, data collection occurs only through third-party services embedded in the site:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google AdSense:</strong> Displays advertising on this site. Google collects usage data, device information, and IP address to serve relevant ads and to measure ad performance. AdSense may use cookies and similar tracking technologies. Google's ad serving and measurement practices are governed by Google's Privacy Policy at <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Analytics:</strong> We use Google Analytics 4 (property G-PW631V2EHR) to collect aggregate traffic data — page views, session duration, geographic region, and device type. This data is used to understand how visitors use the site and to improve content. Google Analytics collects data using cookies and assigns a random client ID to sessions; it does not collect personally identifiable information such as names, email addresses, or phone numbers. Analytics data is aggregate and not tied to individual identities.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How case-review form information is shared</h2>
  <p>If you submit the case-review form, your name, phone number, email address, and case details are shared with one or more attorneys or their agents licensed to practice in your jurisdiction, so they can evaluate your situation and contact you about it. The Click Lab Agency LLC, which operates defamationcalc.com, is not a law firm, does not provide legal advice, and does not vet, endorse, or guarantee the attorneys in this network. Submitting the form does not create an attorney-client relationship with The Click Lab Agency LLC or with any attorney until and unless that attorney separately agrees to represent you. The Click Lab Agency LLC may be compensated for these referrals.</p>
  <p>By submitting the form, you separately consent to be contacted by phone, text, and email — including by automated dialing technology — by The Click Lab Agency LLC and the attorneys or agents your information is shared with. That consent is not required to use any other part of this site, and you can decline it by not submitting the form.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>We do not set first-party cookies beyond what is necessary to record case-review form consent. Google AdSense and Google Analytics set cookies on your device to function. AdSense cookies are used to serve targeted advertising based on your browsing activity. Analytics cookies are used to distinguish sessions and collect aggregate usage data. You can opt out of Google's personalized advertising at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">adssettings.google.com</a>. You can opt out of Google Analytics tracking by installing the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>.</p>

  <h2>How We Use Data</h2>
  <p>The aggregate analytics data collected via Google Analytics is used solely to understand site traffic, identify high-performing content, and improve the editorial quality of the site. We do not sell this analytics data or share it with third parties other than Google as described above.</p>

  <h2>Data Sharing</h2>
  <p>We do not sell, rent, or share visitor data with third parties beyond Google (through AdSense and Analytics, as described above) and, if you submit the case-review form, the attorneys or agents described above. Anonymous browsing of the calculator and guides is never sold or shared, because it collects no personal information in the first place.</p>

  <h2>Your choices and opt-out</h2>
  <p>The simplest opt-out is not to submit the case-review form. If you've already submitted it and want your information removed, or want to withdraw consent to be contacted, email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a> with the subject line <strong>[OPT-OUT]</strong>, or visit <a href="https://theclicklab.agency/optout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">theclicklab.agency/optout</a>.</p>

  <h2>California privacy rights (CCPA/CPRA)</h2>
  <p>Sharing case-review form information with attorneys in exchange for compensation may be considered a &ldquo;sale&rdquo; or &ldquo;share&rdquo; of personal information under the California Consumer Privacy Act and its amendments. California residents may opt out of this sharing at any time using either method above. California residents also have the right to know what personal information we hold, to request deletion, and to non-discrimination for exercising these rights — contact us at the email above to make a request.</p>

  <h2>European privacy rights (GDPR)</h2>
  <p>If you are located in the EU/EEA or UK, the legal basis for processing information you submit through the case-review form is your consent, given at the point of submission. You can withdraw that consent at any time using the opt-out methods above; withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of processing that occurred before withdrawal. Browsing the calculator and guides involves no personal-data processing and requires no legal basis.</p>

  <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
  <p>We do not respond to browser "Do Not Track" signals because we do not directly control the data collection by Google AdSense or Google Analytics. Visitors who wish to limit tracking should use the opt-out mechanisms described in the Cookies section above.</p>

  <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>defamationcalc.com is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect data from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information through this site, contact us at <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>.</p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>We will update this privacy policy when our data practices change. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page reflects the date of the most recent update. Continued use of the site after a policy update constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this privacy policy? Email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>.</p>

  <p>Return to the <a href="/">calculator</a> or see the <a href="/terms/">terms of use</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
